###################################################################################################

###################################
#                                 #
# PREMADE PVP SETS                #
#                                 #
###################################

###################################################################################################
# INFORMATION
#
#

# BT-320, BT-323: a second talent and glyph set per specialization for battlegrounds and arenas. A random bot that
# plays battlegrounds (AiPlayerbot.RandomBotJoinBG) buys Dual Talent Specialization at a class trainer of its class
# with its own gold once it can (level MinDualSpecLevel, 30; 10 gold above its repair reserve), keeps its PvE set in
# the primary talent group and the PvP set below in the secondary one, and switches with the Activate Spec cast (5 s,
# out of combat), as a player does:
#   - to the PvP group when it queues for a battleground or arena or is in a battleground; in an arena only during the
#     preparation phase;
#   - back to the PvE group at the next inn, city or dungeon (out of combat);
#   - the secondary group takes the primary group's specialization; empty tiers and glyphs are filled out of combat;
#     a tier that holds another talent is changed only during a preparation phase, when taking a talent out needs no
#     Tome of the Clear Mind.
# A bot without dual specialization (below level 30, or short of gold) plays matches with its PvE set. Every skill tier
# switches.
#
# AiPlayerbot.PvpTalentSets
#     Description: Random bots buy dual specialization and use the PvP sets below.
#     Default:     1 - on
#                  0 - off (bots play battlegrounds and arenas with their PvE talents)
AiPlayerbot.PvpTalentSets = 1

# AiPlayerbot.PremadeSpecLinkPvp.<class>.<specno> = <tiers>     #same format as PremadeSpecLink; empty = no PvP set
# AiPlayerbot.PremadeSpecGlyphPvp.<class>.<specno> = <glyphs>   #same format as PremadeSpecGlyph
# Every id is checked against the 5.4.8 talent and glyph data (Talent.dbc, GlyphProperties.dbc through the glyph items);
# the comment names each pick. Source: the Skill-Capped MoP Classic PvP guides (patch 5.4.8), the guide's
# default per tier and its three primary major glyphs, alternatives in the comment. Skill-Capped has 16 spec guides; a
# spec without one is marked "unverified" and follows its class's guide for the class-wide talents and glyphs (Icy Veins
# and Archon answer HTTP 403 to automated reads, checked 2026-11-16). Minor glyphs the guide does not list are the PvE
# ones.
# BT-450, BT-453 (2026-11-18): every set was compared with the MoP Classic EU 3v3 ladder, top 100 (96 players, 19
# specializations) and the 2v2 ladder (54 players, 12 specializations); there is no rated battleground data. A pick
# follows the ladder when 60 percent or more of the specialization's players hold another one and it exists on 5.4.8;
# a split pick stays when it is one of the top two. The deciding count is 3v3, or 3v3 plus 2v2 pooled when 3v3 alone has
# under 5 players; a specialization under 5 players even pooled is only noted. One set serves duels (1v1, nearer to 2v2)
# and skirmishes (nearer to 3v3): where the brackets split, the 3v3 pick stays and the line above each set notes the
# 2v2 one. That `ladder` line gives the player counts and what changed.

#
#
#
###################################################################################################

